<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kirtivarman II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 746–753</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kirtivarman II was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukya dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badami">Badami</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramaditya-ii">Vikramaditya II</a> in 746. In 753 his feudatory <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dantidurga">Dantidurga</a> overthrew him and founded the Rashtrakuta dynasty, which took over the Chalukya lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. The Chalukyas returned to power in the 10th century as the Western Chalukyas of Kalyani.</p></div>
